the Meeting Web Portal. Meeting Web Portal . ** Thursday Feb. 12 @ 9:30 am Thursday March 5 @ 9:30 am Thursday April 16 @ 10:00 am Monday May 4 @ 9:00 am Thursday June 4 @ 9:30 am Monday July 14 @ 9:00 am Monday Aug. 3 @ 9:00 am Monday Sept. 14 @ 9:00 am Thursday Oct. 29 @ 9:00 am Nov. No Meeting Monday Dec. 7 @ 9:00 am Chair Dean Crepes Vice Chair Constance Flemming Secretary James Ross Snell Board Member Freddie Black Board Member William Bowman Board Member Robert \u201cBob\u201d Hall Board Member Wyman \u201cBuck\u201d Merchant Board Member James \u201cWhit\u201d Haney Board Member Stacey Faile All dates and times are subject to change; all updates will be posted 72 hours prior to any meeting. Poll worker and Manager information Poll Manager/Poll Manager Assistant (Student) Application and Information (PDF) Poll Clerk Application and Information (PDF) Precincts for the upcoming Nov 3rd election Election Nov 3, 2026- Precinct Notice (PDF) Find Poll locations Election Information Registrations & Elections Board Member Log in to MyscVOTES (My Registration, My Sample Ballot, My Polling Place, My Voting History) Registration and Election Board Meeting Agenda ( September 14th, 2026 ) County of Lexington Registration and Election Auxiliary Administration Building 605 West Main Street, Suite C, Lexington, SC 29072 Contact: Phone: (803) 785-8361 Contact Information Lenice Shoemaker , Director County of Lexington Registration and Election Auxiliary Administration Building 605 West Main Street, Suite C Lexington, SC 29072 Phone: (803) 785-8361 SC Voter ID Law \u201cGo to SCVOTES.GOV or Call the Lexington County Voter Registration Office to confirm that you are eligible to vote in this Election\u201d Early voting allows registered voters to cast their ballot in person before Election Day. During the early voting period, voters may visit any early voting center in their county, present a valid photo ID, and vote using the same system used on Election Day. For more information, please view the Early Voting Brochure or visit Early Voting at scVOTES.gov. Absentee Voting Absentee voting allows eligible voters to cast their ballot either by mail or in person before Election Day. It is available to voters who meet certain qualifying criteria set by state law. For more information, please view the Absentee Voting Brochure or visit Absentee Voting at scVOTES.gov. Public Notices: Statewide General Election Go to Guide (PDF) Absentee Statewide General Election Go to Guide (PDF) PUBLIC Testing Notice- NOV 3 2026 (PDF) Republican Runoff Primary Unofficial Election Results (PDF) Republican Special Primary Official Election Results (PDF) Public Notice Watershed District Directors November 3, 2026 General Election (PDF) 2026 SC Watershed District Election Memo (PDF) Elections Dates 2026 August - November November General Election Early Voting: Monday - Saturday Monday, October 19, 2026 - Saturday, October 31, 2026 8:30 a.m. - 6:00 p.m. Election Day: Tuesday, November 3, 2026 7:00 a.m. - 7:00 p.m. Run-Off: (TBD) November 17 Next Council Meeting Information on upcoming Council meetings, Committee meetings and Public Hearings. Learn More HUD Grant Programs Information on CDBG, HOME, ESG, Disaster Recovery/Mitigation, Covid-19 Learn More Transparency Reports Reports prepared each month at the Fund, Department, and Transaction levels. Learn More Facebook Page Twitter Feed County of Lexington 212 South Lake Drive Lexington, SC 29072 803-359-8000 Footer menu Privacy Policy Disclaimer Contact SC.GOV Home SC.GOV Privacy & Security Policy Help Center Contact SC.GOV Download Adobe Reader Copyright \u00a9 State of South Carolina",
